Section 4 : Chunk Enrichment
✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ ✅ 

>> What is Chunk Enrichment?

When large documents are split into smaller pieces called chunks, the chunks can be enhanced with additional information before storing them in a search index. This process is called Chunk Enrichment.

Instead of storing only the chunk text, we store:

1. Extracted entities
2. Key phrases
3. Metadata
4. Security information
5. Redacted content

This makes search and retrieval far more accurate.


 🔹 1. PII Detection and Redaction
	What is PII? Personally Identifiable Information (PII) is any information that can identify a person.

	Examples: Full Name, Email Address

 🔹 2. NER (Named Entity Recognition)
	What is NER?  --> NER identifies important real-world objects mentioned in the text and categorizes them.

  🔹 3. Key-Phrase Extraction
    What is it?  ---> Key-phrase extraction automatically identifies the most important topics from a document.
		
















































































